# TRINAMIC_TMC2160A_TA — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# NEW PART (2026-07-26, middleweight capture). Stepper driver IC for the Middleweight's
# motor stage: direct-mode (register 0x2D) drive of 8x external 100V N-FETs (2 full
# H-bridges), SPI configuration, dual current-sense amplifiers, integrated gate drivers +
# charge pump. LCSC C465948 (TMC2160A-TA-T — "-T" is the tape&reel packaging suffix on the
# same base part the brief names "TMC2160A-TA"), TQFP-48-EP (7x7mm body / 9x9mm with
# leads). Stock 4,431 units @ $6.71-$4.07 (checked 2026-07-26) — Extended (no BASIC-class
# high-current stepper driver exists at this tier; matches the brief's own "Extended
# (VERIFY)" flag). JLC also lists the same base part under C1161715 (TQFP-48-EP,
# Economic/Standard SMT) — same physical device, C465948 used here since its stock+price
# were independently confirmed.
#
# DATASHEET FINDINGS (TRINAMIC TMC2160 datasheet Rev 1.01, 2018-OKT-29 — the TMC2160A
# shares this pinout/electrical spec per the combined ADI/TRINAMIC "TMC2160/TMC2160A"
# datasheet; full pin table + electrical characteristics read, not assumed):
# - DRV_ENN (pin 28) has NO internal pull resistor (confirmed from the pin table — many
#   TMC2160 pins are marked "(pd)"/"(pu)", DRV_ENN is not) — an EXTERNAL pull-up is
#   mandatory to get "default = disabled" per the safety brief; this board provides one.
# - Gate driver current vs DRVSTRENGTH: 200/400/600mA (low-side) and 150/300/450mA
#   (high-side) @ DRVSTRENGTH=0/2/3. MOSFET Miller-charge table: Qgd 20-40nC -> DRVSTRENGTH
#   1 or 2, RG <=7.5R. The board's FET (HUAYI_HYG053N10NS1C2, Qgd=23nC, Qg_total=73nC) sits
#   in this bucket — comfortably within the driver's capability, no second FET P/N needed.
# - VSA/VS operating range 10-50/10-55V, abs max 60V (peak 64V incl. charge-pump coupling).
#   Datasheet Section 3.2 flags: "with MOSFETs above 50nC of total gate charge... it is
#   recommended to use a VSA supply not higher than 40V" (or feed an external 12V gate
#   supply, Fig 3.2) to limit internal-regulator self-heating. This board's FET is 73nC
#   (>50nC) and VSA is tied to the 46V bus (>40V) — the STANDARD circuit (VSA=VS, internal
#   11.5V/5V regulators, Fig 3.1) is used here since no 12V rail exists in the locked power
#   tree; flagged for Ben as a bring-up thermal item (see middleweight.zen comment at the
#   TMC2160A instantiation and the session report) — not a functional blocker, the internal
#   regulator still operates correctly at 48V, just with reduced thermal margin.
# - Charge pump: VCP-VS = V12VOUT-[1,2] when operating; CPI/CPO need a 22nF/100V cap (Fig
#   2.1 standard app circuit); VCP needs a 100nF cap to VS.
# - Absolute max BM pins (bridge-center) -6V to VVS+6V (stray-inductance ringing budget).
HB1 = io("HB1", Net, optional = True)
CB1 = io("CB1", Net, optional = True)
v12out = io("v12out", Net, optional = True)
VSA = io("VSA", Net, optional = True)
v5out = io("v5out", Net, optional = True)
